{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q1820045","formula":"CaGd₂(UO₂)₂₄(CO₃)₈Si₄O₂₈·60H₂O","hill":"C8H120CaGd2O160Si4U24","elements":["H","C","O","Si","Ca","Gd","U"],"composition":{"C":8.0,"H":120.0,"O":160.0,"U":24.0,"Ca":1.0,"Gd":2.0,"Si":4.0},"names":{"en":"Lepersonnite-(Gd)","uk":"Леперсоніт-(Gd)"},"descriptions":{"en":"Lepersonnite-(Gd) is a very rare uranium and rare-earth mineral with the chemical formula Ca(Gd,Dy)2(UO2)24(SiO4)4(CO3)8(OH)24·48H2O. It occurs with bijvoetite-(Y) in the Shinkolobwe deposit in the Democratic Republic of the Congo, famous for rare uranium minerals. It was the first confirmed mineral with essential gadolinium and remained the only gadolinium dominant species until the description of Monazite-(Gd) in 2023. It was first described in 1982 and is named after the Belgian geologist Jacques Lepersonne.","uk":"Леперсоніт-(Gd) — рідкісний рідкісноземельний мінерал урану з хімічною формулою Ca(Gd,Dy)2(UO2)24(SiO4)4(CO3)8(OH)24·48H2O. Він проявляється з біжветитом-(Y) у родовищі Шинколобве в Демократичній Республіці Конго, відомому рідкісними мінералами урану. Донедавна це був єдиний підтверджений мінерал з незамінним гадолінієм у складі. Названий на честь бельгійського геолога Жака Леперсонна."},"fame":10,"pubchemCid":null,"mass":null,"charge":0,"smiles":null,"inchikey":null,"iupac":null,"classes":[{"qid":"Q12089225","names":{"en":"mineral species","ru":"действительный вид минералов","uk":"мінеральний вид"}}],"structureInfo":null,"structure":null,"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q1820045","license":"CC0 1.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (en)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lepersonnite-%28Gd%29","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (uk)","url":"https://uk.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%9B%D0%B5%D0%BF%D0%B5%D1%80%D1%81%D0%BE%D0%BD%D1%96%D1%82-%28Gd%29","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"photo","name":"Wikimedia Commons","url":"https://commons.wikimedia.org